; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Population Growth
; CATEGORY: Science & Simulation
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     biology, growth, exponential, logistic, graph
; SUMMARY:  Compares a population that grows without limits to one that runs short of food, as two curves on a graph.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Imagine a jar of fruit flies. Each day the population grows by 30
;   percent. The red curve shows what happens if food never runs out:
;   it shoots off the top of the screen. The blue curve shows what
;   really happens in a jar: growth slows down as the food gets scarce,
;   and the number levels off at what the jar can support.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Read the day-by-day table in the text window too.
;   Change GROWTH or CAPACITY at the bottom and run again.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * exponential growth: multiplying again and again
;   * logistic growth: growth that slows near a limit
;   * MAKE to update a variable each time round a loop
;   * REPCOUNT to know which day we are on
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make GROWTH 0.1. How long until the flies reach the limit now?
;   * Start with 200 flies instead of 10.
;   * Halve the CAPACITY halfway through, as if half the food spoiled.
; ============================================================

; The graph: day 0 is at x = -350, and each day is 18 steps to the right.
; One fly is 0.5 steps tall, so 1000 flies is 500 steps.
to day.x :day
  output -350 + :day * 18
end

to flies.y :n
  output -250 + :n * 0.5
end

to draw.axes
  setpc 0 setpensize 1
  penup setxy -350 -250 pendown setx 390
  penup setxy -350 -250 pendown sety 280
  ; a dashed line at the jar's limit
  setpc 15
  penup setxy -350 flies.y :capacity
  setheading 90
  repeat 37 [pendown fd 10 penup fd 10]
  setpc 0 penup setxy -340 (flies.y :capacity) + 6
  label [the most flies the jar can feed]
  penup setxy 350 -275 label [days]
  setxy -345 285 label [flies]
end

to grow :days
  localmake "free 10        ; flies with unlimited food
  localmake "jar 10         ; flies in a real jar
  print "|day   unlimited  in the jar|
  repeat :days [
    ; Unlimited: every day there are 30 percent more flies.
    make "free :free + :growth * :free
    ; In the jar the growth is multiplied by the share of food left.
    ; Near the limit that share is close to zero, so growth stops.
    make "jar :jar + :growth * :jar * (1 - :jar / :capacity)
    ; FORM pads each number to a fixed width so the columns line up
    print (word form repcount 3 0 form :free 12 0 form :jar 12 0)
    ; a red dot for unlimited, while it still fits on the screen
    if (flies.y :free) < 290 [
      setpc 4 penup setxy day.x repcount flies.y :free dot pos
    ]
    setpc 1 penup setxy day.x repcount flies.y :jar dot pos
    wait 8
  ]
end

make "growth 0.3
make "capacity 800

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground 7
setlabelheight 14
draw.axes
setpensize 8
grow 40
penup setxy 100 -100 setpc 4 label [red: unlimited food]
setxy 100 -125 setpc 1 label [blue: flies in a jar]
